==Changelog September 25th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''Varlamore: The Rising Darkness'''

* New parts of Varlamore are now available to explore! Main features include:
** Multiple new quests including The Heart of Darkness and Death on the Isle.
** Hueycoatl, a new group boss.
** Mastering Mixology, a new Herblore activity.
** The Colossal Wyrm Agility Course.
** ... and more!

'''Araxxor'''

* Updated the descriptions of the Perfect Araxxor combat task to include the fail conditions.
* Renamed the 'Relaxed Gamer' task to 'Relaxxor'.

'''Other Changes'''

* Adjusted the Inquisitor Armour's Damage and Accuracy bonus to Crush. Now, each Inquisitor Armour piece (Plateskirt, Helmet, Hauberk) gives +2.5% Crush Accuracy and Damage when used alongside the Inquisitor's Mace, regardless of set effects.
* Enabled the ability to toggle Run to ‘Always On’.
* The quest journal will now remain open when moving around and will also resize on larger screen sizes.
* You will now get a warning when dropping items in the Giants' Foundry during the Sleeping Giants quest.
* The flames on the Leagues IV: Trailblazer Reloaded trophies are now animated.
* Bridge Guard no longer spots the player at the safe spot near the north-western bridge during the Stealing Artifacts minigame.
* Farmers now have trade options which use the standard shop interface.
* Reduced the aggression radius of ancient wyverns.
* Making Ultracompost now gives token Farming XP.
* The S.T.A.S.H. unit at the top of the Watchtower can once again be used for storage before the quest is complete. This does not affect the quest requirement for the clue.

'''PvP Rota'''

The PvP rota has moved to '''Period B''':

* 560 - (UK) - PvP World
* 319 - (US) - Bounty Hunter World
* 579 - (US) - High-Risk PvP World
* 561 - (UK) - Free-to-Play PvP World
* 580 - (US) - LMS Competitive

World 390 (AUS) for LMS Competitive has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

World 569 (AUS) for Bounty Hunter has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

The PvP Arena is using '<b>Max/Med</b>' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week.

